    "root_cause_analysis": "The 65 alert records generated 13,532 unique flow IDs because Vertical Port Scan (RULE_PORT_SCAN_VERTICAL) from attacker 172.16.0.1 grouped 10,263 single-packet scan flows into 1 alert, and Excessive Connection Attempts (RULE_EXCESSIVE_CONN_RATE) from 172.16.0.1 grouped 2,210 DDoS flows into 1 alert. Conversely, the 45 DNS alerts operate purely on DnsQueryRecord and attach 0 flow IDs. Horizontal sweep rules (RULE_PORT_SCAN_HORIZONTAL) triggered on normal workstations visiting multi-host web endpoints, generating 943 false-positive flow IDs."
